{{Quote|Now we must leave, before more security droids arrive.|[[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]]|<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref>}}
'''Security droids''',<ref name="Droidography">''[[Star Wars: Droidography]]''</ref> also known as '''enforcer droids''',<ref name="USE">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Ultimate Sticker Encyclopedia]]''</ref> were a type of [[droid]] used for supervision and enforcement, often relying on brute strength.<ref name="Droidography" />

==History==
During the [[Battle of Jedha]], [[Eiram's military]] made use of enforcer droids supplied by [[Tilson Graf]], who in secret was partnered with [[Elecia Zeveron|the Mother]] of the [[Path of the Open Hand]]. Graf also supplied a shipment of enforcer droids to the Mother to protect the Path.<ref name="Battle of Jedha">''[[The High Republic: The Battle of Jedha]]''</ref> The Path of the Open Hand, which transformed into the [[Path of the Closed Fist]], made use of the enforcer droids during the [[Night of Sorrow]].<ref name="Vengeance">''[[The High Republic: Path of Vengeance]]''</ref> During the [[Clone Wars]], the term "security droid" commonly referred to the [[OOM-series security droid]]<ref name="Episode III" /> used by the [[Trade Federation]]<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="Episode III" /> [[Owen Lars]] had a [[KPR security droid]] at his [[moisture farm]].<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref>

[[File:EntertheKXDroids.png|thumb|left|300px|The KX-series "security" droid was a battle droid in all but name.]]
The [[KX-series security droid|KX-series]] was a security droid model used by the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> An offshoot of the droid-based [[Droid Gotra]] crime family,<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> the [[Vanguard Axis]] was an entirely-droid run cartel<ref name="SWECG">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> whose number included a great many [[K3 security droid]]s.<ref name="Tribe">{{TBB|Tribe}}</ref> The [[Crimson Dawn]] syndicate used modified [[A3L-N sentinel droid|A3L-N sentinel droids]] to patrol a [[prison]] area on Crimson Dawn's [[fortress]] [[flagship]] [[Vermillion (Crimson Dawn)|''Vermillion'']].<ref name="Aphra 14">[[Doctor Aphra (2020) 14|''Doctor Aphra'' (2020) 14]]</ref> The [[New Republic]] used [[N5 sentry droid]]s and [[R1 security droid]]s.<ref name="Mando 6">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 6: The Prisoner}}</ref> The [[First Order]] was known to use the [[KXFO-series security droid]].<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> A model of [[Security droid (Colossus)|security droid]] was stationed aboard the refueling station known as the ''[[Colossus]]'' during [[34 ABY]], where they ensured peace onboard at the will of [[Captain]] [[Imanuel Doza]].<ref name="The High Tower">{{Resistance|The High Tower}}</ref> Doza’s droid assistant [[4D-M1N]] kept track of the security droids, and was alerted if they were ever deactivated.<ref name="The Doza Dilemma">{{Resistance|The Doza Dilemma}}</ref>

